message: "If you use QSOL-SUBSTRATE, please cite the archived software release and retain the exact version/commit identity."
title: "QSOL-SUBSTRATE: A Deterministic, Provenance-Aware Public Context Substrate for AI Systems"
type: software
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-08-15
commit: 4483582173abf62f61bcc18076b22c1db10b26ca
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/QSOLKCB/QSOL-SUBSTRATE"
repository-artifact: "https://github.com/QSOLKCB/QSOL-SUBSTRATE/releases/tag/v1.0.0"
abstract: >-
  QSOL-SUBSTRATE is a public, vendor-neutral context substrate for AI systems.
  It provides deterministic, provenance-aware context for identity, terminology,
  projects, publications, relationships, chronology, and epistemic state while
  preserving strict separation between canonical public facts and derived
  adapters, tool-less capsules, vector indexes, latent/prefix experiments,
  evaluation reports, release manifests, and archival metadata. Version 1.0.0
  completes the Phase 0-8 roadmap and includes the 48-case Substrate Probe and
  YEAH-NAH/1 Australian-pragmatics suite. Its central semantic rule is that
  absence from the public substrate means unavailable, not false.
